 "notes": "Stretch 1. p.118: started at the row below the long rule (y~660) 're en unt reṭ ...'; four rows above not read. The rule directly above that row runs from x~236 (just right of '1.') to x~915, ending before Àusàr: taken as an overline (rubric) over the title re ... t'eṭ àn; likewise on p.119 the rule above the Chapter VIII title runs from x~206 to x~867 over re ... àn, ending before Àusàr. No other overlines seen on pp.118-119. Line numerals LXXIV: '1.' before re (p.118 r1); '2.' before em (p.118 r3, after reṭ-à); '3.' inside χu between the ibis and the chick (p.118 r4) - χu kept in line 2; '4.' inside ḥer between D2/Z1 and D21 at the end of p.118 r5 - ḥer kept in line 3; p.119 r1-2 (ābeḥ ... ḥetep) line 4. VIII: '1.' before title (p.119 r3); '2.' before ṭep (r4); '3.' after Rā (r6); '4.' before àm (r7). Dots: p.119 r4 Budge prints 'ṭep....' ; p.119 r5 he prints '....' under a lone kneeling man before 'em' and '....' in the English (recorded as a separate word with budge '....'). Brackets in the sign line p.119: [re] r1; [re en] r3 title; [pert] r3; [nuk] r6; [àm] r6; [O4] and [G43 N5] in hru-f r7. No footnotes on these pages. t'eṭ àn has no separate English for àn (gloss left empty)."
